 ### [MultiPlaneNeRF](8875-multiplanenerf.md)
-MultiPlaneNeRF is a radiance field representation that replaces the trainable implicit encoding of vanilla NeRF with a non-trainable 2D image-based representation. It solves the problems of long training times and poor generalization to unseen data by projecting 3D points onto a set of 2D images to form an aggregate feature vector, which is then decoded by a small, shallow implicit network. Unlike vanilla NeRF, which requires separate training for each object and encodes geometry in weights, MultiPlaneNeRF allows a single decoder to generalize across many objects by simply swapping the input 2D image planes. It is chosen for generalizable novel view synthesis across multiple objects. [MultiPlaneNeRF](8875-multiplanenerf.md)
