 ### [MS-NeRF](9111-ms-nerf.md)
-MS-NeRF (Multi-Space Neural Radiance Field) is a scene representation method that extends standard MLP-based NeRF architectures to handle unbounded virtual scenes containing reflective and refractive surfaces, such as mirrors. It solves the problem of rendering distortion and blurring caused by reflection or refraction, where standard NeRF fails to maintain multi-view consistency due to the geometric complexity of virtual images. Unlike sibling methods like Ref-NeRF, which require manually labeled masks for reflective surfaces and are limited to forward-facing scenes, MS-NeRF automatically handles 360-degree scenes without extra supervision. It sets itself apart by decomposing the radiance field into $K$ parallel sub-spaces, each representing a characteristic field, and integrating them via a learned gating mechanism. It is chosen for scenes with complex reflections and refractions. [MS-NeRF](9111-ms-nerf.md)
