 ### [RING-NeRF](9323-ring-nerf.md)
-RING-NeRF is a neural field architecture that introduces two primary inductive biases: a continuous multi-scale scene representation and a decoder latent space invariant to spatial translations and scale changes. Unlike sibling methods such as [Zip-NeRF](8663-nerf-rpn.md) or [Mip-NeRF](8875-multiplanenerf.md) which require explicit supervision for Level of Detail (LOD) or modify features based on observation distance, RING-NeRF produces intrinsic continuous LOD without supervision, enabling robust generalization to novel, unseen observation distances. It distinguishes itself from [I-NGP](8953-pool-proposer-architecture.md) by using summation rather than concatenation for multi-resolution features, ensuring the decoder latent space remains invariant to LOD, and supports dynamic resolution extension during training. It is chosen for generalizable NeRF with continuous LOD. [RING-NeRF](9323-ring-nerf.md)
