 ### [IRON](10251-iron.md)
-IRON is a neural inverse rendering pipeline that reconstructs high-quality 3D geometry and spatially varying materials from photometric images (captured with a collocated flashlight and moving camera). It outputs triangle meshes and material textures suitable for standard graphics pipelines. Unlike methods that optimize surface representations directly, IRON employs a hybrid optimization scheme: it first uses volumetric radiance field rendering to recover correct object topology, then refines geometry and disentangles materials from lighting using edge-aware physics-based surface rendering. This two-stage approach prevents divergence and local minima associated with direct surface optimization. It is chosen for inverse rendering with material estimation. [IRON](10251-iron.md)
