 ### [pi-GAN](10298-pi-gan.md)
-pi-GAN is a generative adversarial network that learns an unsupervised, 3D-aware implicit radiance field from 2D images by conditioning a SIREN network on a latent noise vector. It differs from standard NeRF training by treating the radiance field as a generative prior conditioned on a global shape/appearance code $z$, rather than optimizing a specific scene's coordinates directly, and by using a mapping network with Feature-wise Linear Modulation (FiLM) instead of simple concatenation. Unlike GRAF, which uses concatenation-based conditioning and patch-based discriminators, pi-GAN employs a StyleGAN-inspired mapping network and a global convolutional discriminator to avoid local overfitting inherent to periodic activations. It is chosen for 3D-aware generation with style control. [pi-GAN](10298-pi-gan.md)
