 ### [MIMO-NeRF](10928-mimo-nerf.md)
-MIMO-NeRF is a neural rendering method that accelerates inference by replacing the standard Single-Input Single-Output (SISO) Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP) with a Multi-Input Multi-Output (MIMO) MLP. It groups neighboring samples along a ray and processes them simultaneously, reducing the number of MLP evaluations (# Run) required per pixel. Unlike knowledge distillation methods that require training a separate teacher network, MIMO-NeRF can be trained via self-supervised learning using a 3D consistency loss to resolve ambiguities in density and color inherent in grouped predictions. It maintains the original NeRF hyperparameters (sample counts and network width) while achieving superior speed-quality trade-offs compared to methods that reduce sample counts or network width. It is chosen for inference acceleration without distillation. [MIMO-NeRF](10928-mimo-nerf.md)
