 ### [Quadri-Plane Radiance Fields](11128-quadri-plane-radiance-fields.md)
-Quadri-Plane Radiance Fields represent a 3D scene using four multi-channel 2D feature planes coupled with a lightweight decoder MLP, designed to enable computationally efficient volumetric super-resolution by leveraging 2D image super-resolution techniques. Unlike standard NeRF implementations that rely on dense 3D voxel grids or large MLPs for all features, this method decouples spatial geometry and view-dependent appearance into explicit 2D planes, allowing the use of established 2D SR architectures for upscaling. It sets itself apart from siblings like [HexPlane](11358-hexplane.md) by using exactly four axis-aligned planes (three positional, one directional) rather than six, and from [Sparse and Efficient Representations](9326-sparse-and-efficient-representations.md) by maintaining a dense, fixed-resolution plane structure optimized for low-resolution input scaling. It is chosen for efficient super-resolution. [Quadri-Plane Radiance Fields](11128-quadri-plane-radiance-fields.md)
