-### [HexPlane](11358-hexplane.md)
-HexPlane is an explicit representation for dynamic 3D scenes that decomposes a 4D spacetime grid into six feature planes spanning each pair of coordinate axes (e.g., XY, ZT). It computes features for points in spacetime by projecting the point onto each feature plane, aggregating the six resulting feature vectors, and passing the fused vector to a tiny MLP to predict color. This method solves the problem of efficient novel view synthesis for dynamic scenes by avoiding the high computational cost of implicit MLP-based representations and the memory inefficiency of dense 4D grids. It sets itself apart from implicit methods (like T-NeRF) by using an explicit factorized structure, achieving comparable or better synthesis quality with over 100× acceleration. It is chosen for dynamic scene rendering. [HexPlane](11358-hexplane.md)
+GNeuVox is a differentiable volume rendering framework for fast human radiance field optimization that replaces implicit MLPs with explicit neural voxel grids to accelerate training from hours to minutes. It distinguishes itself by maintaining two separate voxel grids: general voxels ($V_g$) pretrained across multiple subjects to provide geometric priors, and individual voxels ($V_i$) optimized per subject to capture unique differential textures. This separation allows the model to converge rapidly during fine-tuning while maintaining rendering quality comparable to methods requiring significantly longer training times. See [GNeuVox](11357-gneuvox.md).
 
 ### [STensoRRF](11359-stensorrf.md)
-STensoRRF is a differentiable volume rendering method that represents a 3D scene using a single 4D tensor to enable high-quality novel view synthesis and relighting. It distinguishes itself from standard NeRF architectures by replacing the multi-network feature grid with a decomposed single tensor and explicitly estimating a BRDF value per point to facilitate relighting via spherical Gaussian environment maps. Unlike sibling methods that rely on complex geometric priors or multiple voxel meshes, STensoRRF achieves a 50% faster convergence rate and 1.5x faster rendering speed by combining tensor decomposition with a simplified reflectance equation. It is chosen for relighting and efficient tensor-based representation. [STensoRRF](11359-stensorrf.md)
