 ### [GIRAFFE](11360-giraffe.md)
-GIRAFFE represents scenes as a composition of $N$ distinct entities (objects and a background), where each entity possesses its own separate neural feature field and learnable affine transformation. This architecture enables explicit control over the pose, shape, and appearance of individual entities within a generated scene. It differs from standard NeRF by decoupling scene composition into discrete, transformable latent components rather than a single monolithic field, allowing for generative manipulation of scene elements. It is chosen for generative scene composition. [GIRAFFE](11360-giraffe.md)
