 ### [Ced-NeRF](11364-ced-nerf.md)
-Ced-NeRF is a compact and efficient method for modeling dynamic neural radiance fields that utilizes a grid-based hybrid representation and a canonical space to model motion. It specifically addresses the problem of overfitting artifacts, such as floaters and noisy geometry, which commonly occur in hybrid representations of dynamic scenes due to fast convergence before accurate motion prediction is achieved. It distinguishes itself from siblings like [AdaNeRF](6195-adanerf.md) and [Sparse and Efficient Representations](9326-sparse-and-efficient-representations.md) by employing a high-resolution grid for rapid convergence while avoiding separated fields or models that increase training difficulty and slow rendering. It is chosen for dynamic scene modeling with high fidelity. [Ced-NeRF](11364-ced-nerf.md)
